<div id="2026-09-30-ollama-systemone-client" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-30 — Ollama SystemOne client (local decision models) + the 0.35 install defect it exposed</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added the SystemOne/decision client: <code>Comserv::Model::Ollama::Decision</code> (new role, composed into <code>Model::Ollama</code>) posts to <code>/v1/systemone</code> and returns typed answers with probabilities and confidence; <code>Model::AI2::Provider::Ollama::decide</code> is the v2 wrapper with the same reachability fail-fast and a 900s cold timeout that <code>chat</code> uses. Accessors <code>systemone_choice</code>/<code>systemone_noul</code>/<code>systemone_score</code> keep callers from re-implementing the answer shapes, and requests are validated client-side (1–64 questions, choice 2–255 options, score 2–10 levels) so a malformed call never leaves the app. New <code>t/ollama_decision.t</code> (76 tests) and <code>script/ollama_decision_probe.pl</code> for live proof. This is AISYSTEMPlan 5f step 2; no consumer is rewired yet.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Every triage/routing/classification job currently asks a generative model to emit JSON in prose and then parses it. SystemOne computes the answer from the model's probabilities and returns a value, so there is nothing to parse and off-schema output is impossible — for free, locally, in ~4s (tev1:0.8b) instead of an external hop.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Also fixed, same day.</strong> The Ollama 0.35.0 upgrade had written <code>bin/ollama</code> correctly but silently failed to unpack <code>lib/ollama</code> — only <code>cuda_v12/libggml-cuda.so</code> landed, so <code>llama-server</code> and the ggml libraries were missing and every local model failed with <em>llama-server binary not found</em>. It passed review because <code>ollama --version</code> reported 0.35.0 and <code>ollama list</code> showed the new models. Re-extracted the official release tarball (sha256 verified against the release <code>sha256sum.txt</code>) into <code>/usr/local/lib/ollama</code>; no service restart needed since llama-server is exec'd per request. Full record on todo #2528, which stays open for the missing post-install assert.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Ollama/Decision.pm</code> (new), <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Ollama.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Provider/Ollama.pm</code>, <code>t/ollama_decision.t</code> (new), <code>script/ollama_decision_probe.pl</code> (new). Docs: <code>root/Documentation/AISYSTEMPlan.tt</code> §5f.</p>
</div>
